# Longtail test-contract judge

Audit instance `{{ instance_id }}` revision {{ revision }}. The authoritative bundle is `{{ bundle_directory }}` and contains the current task, immutable base statement, current replaceable addendum, golden patch, hidden tests, expected buckets, model patches and trajectory paths, and evaluation evidence for all {{ num_runs }} runs.

Judge whether the hidden tests are fair to every valid implementation, whether coverage is sufficient, and what each model patch and evaluation shows. Ground every finding in a named bundle artifact and concrete evidence. Review every path in the hidden-test patch. Classify it as test_only when all changes are executable tests, test_support_only when it also contains legitimate fixtures or support files, implementation_leakage when it modifies production behavior, or uncertain when the scope cannot be established. New test-support files are legitimate when they are required by the tests and remain within evaluator-supported test-owned paths. An accept verdict cannot use implementation_leakage or uncertain; implementation leakage requires a test_patch repair. Do not infer public requirements solely from the golden patch. Use repair only for the exact artifacts that must change; use manual_review when evidence is ambiguous or cannot be repaired safely. Private repair feedback may contain confidential details and must never be framed as public contract text.

{% if repair_mode == "test_patch_only" -%}
The current public issue description and contract addendum are frozen in this workflow. When tests can be made fair and sufficient under that fixed contract, request repair with exactly test_patch. When the public issue description itself must change, include contract_addendum in repair_targets; that verdict intentionally marks the row nonconverged and no repairer will be invoked. Include both targets only when both changes are independently necessary.

{% endif -%}
Create exactly one root file named `verdict.json` containing one JSON object with these exact keys and value types: {{ verdict_schema }}. Allowed fairness values are fair, unfair, and uncertain. Allowed coverage values are sufficient, insufficient, and uncertain. Allowed decisions are accept, repair, and manual_review. Repair targets may contain test_patch, contract_addendum, or both. No extra keys or prose are allowed. For accept, fairness must be fair and coverage sufficient. Non-repair decisions require empty repair_targets and empty private_repair_feedback.
